; ==========================================================================
; STELLAR BIG CLOCK v2  -  seven-segment clock, hourly chime, alarm   (loads at $4000)
; ==========================================================================
; NEEDS THE $07 RTC OPCODE (V0061.35). Sound: a speaker or buzzer on Q.
;
; The time as six big seven-segment digits (HH:MM:SS, 24-hour) in reverse-video blocks,
; the day of the week below, the date ("October 2, 2026") below that; the chime and alarm
; settings under the title. Plain VT100; nothing scrolls; only changed digit rows are sent.
;
;   S  set the clock: date YYYY-MM-DD, time HH:MM:SS (the firmware checks every field)
;   A  set the alarm: HH:MM (Enter alone = alarm off)
;   C  hourly chime on/off: strikes the hour, 1-12 (15:00 = 3), one strike a second
;   Q  quit (Esc too)
; When the alarm goes off: four short high beeps every second and ALARM on screen until a
; key - Z snoozes 9 minutes, any other key stops it (it goes off again tomorrow).
; The chime and alarm settings are kept in memory: they survive Q and a rerun, not a reload
; or power-off. They start OFF.
;
; Chime 518 Hz, 0.3 s a strike; alarm 1003 Hz.
;
; VERIFICATION (Firmware-Math/bigclock2_verify.py, V0061.34 + RTC-07): ALL PASS 2026-10-03 (digits read back off a strict VT100 screen; Q measured in machine cycles): v1's display tests (Elf2K BIOS mode, <=325 bytes a second, midnight/New Year, set + refused + cancel, never-set chip, quit + rerun); chime: 3 strikes at 15:00, 0.30 s at 518 Hz, one a second, none at start-up or after setting; alarm: rings at 07:31 (4 beeps a second, 1003 Hz), Z snoozes to 07:40 and rings again, another key stops it, next alarm 07:31; 25:00 refused; Enter = off; settings kept over Q + rerun, garbage = off; 60 typed characters cannot overrun.
;
; 589 STELLAR commands, 1774 bytes of code + 320 bytes of native 1802 code; the program block
; is used to $4F8D.
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

; D 4000 CD             START
